# Copy to .dev.vars (gitignored) and fill in. LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS FOR. wrangler/miniflare reads .dev.vars under `astro dev`
# and `wrangler dev` and binds every line into the Worker environment, the same
# way `wrangler secret` binds a value in a real deployment. Nothing here is
# compiled into a bundle.
#
# WHY IT IS NOT .env. Vite replaces the whole `import.meta.env` expression with
# an object literal holding every variable .env carried, so anything read that
# way is a plaintext literal inside dist/server. The routes that read the
# environment — src/pages/api/cron/digest.ts, src/pages/app/setup.astro,
# src/lib/billing/config.ts — read `cloudflare:workers` and fall back to
# `process.env`, neither of which Vite touches. The cost is that .env does not
# reach the Worker in local dev. This file does.
#
# .env keeps the PUBLIC_* values and everything Node-side reads directly:
# tests (tests/helpers.ts parses it), migrations, the deploy scripts.

# THE SEND GUARD. KEEP IT, AND KEEP IT FIRST.
#
# `astro dev` loads wrangler.jsonc — the PRODUCTION config — which sets
# DEPLOY_ENV to "production". src/lib/notify/guard.ts treats that as the one
# value that permits sending to a real recipient, so without this line a local
# run mails real carriers about deadlines that are not theirs. Everything else
# in this file is what makes sending possible, so a missing .dev.vars leaves a
# clone unable to send at all rather than able to send to the wrong people.
DEPLOY_ENV=development

# Scheduled jobs. Without it /api/cron/digest refuses to run rather than
# defaulting to unauthenticated.
CRON_SECRET=
# The one legitimate privileged key: a cron run has no signed-in user and must
# read across every carrier.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# USDOT claim verification, at least 32 characters, DIFFERENT in every
# environment. Without it /app/setup cannot mint a code and says so.
CLAIM_CODE_PEPPER=

# Outbound email and SMS. While DEPLOY_ENV is not "production" every message is
# redirected to the two addresses below, and if those are blank nothing is sent.
RESEND_API_KEY=
DIGEST_FROM_EMAIL=
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER=
DEV_REDIRECT_EMAIL=
DEV_REDIRECT_PHONE=

# SUPABASE AUTH EMAIL — the value that brings signup, password reset and email
# change under the guard above.
#
# Generated by the Supabase dashboard at Authentication -> Hooks -> Send Email,
# in the shape `v1,whsec_<base64>`. Paste it whole; src/lib/auth/email-hook.ts
# strips the prefix and base64-decodes the rest into the HMAC key.
#
# With the hook enabled, Supabase stops sending auth email itself and POSTs it to
# /api/auth/email instead, which sends it through send() — so DEPLOY_ENV and
# DEV_REDIRECT_EMAIL apply to it exactly as they apply to the digest. Without
# this value that endpoint REFUSES every request rather than sending unverified
# mail, which means auth email stops. Set it in the same breath as enabling the
# hook, never before and never after.
SEND_EMAIL_HOOK_SECRET=

# Stripe, read by src/lib/billing/config.ts. Test-mode values only here:
# readStripeConfig refuses an sk_live_ key wherever DEPLOY_ENV is not
# "production". Leave blank to run with card payment switched off.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_PRICE_ID=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
